\tag{fdip}
\title{Group-algebra sectors}
\date{2026-10-20}

\p{How can the same half-turn act on different Gaussian states?
The [group-algebra extension](fdip-003N) and its
[module projectors](fdip-003O) separate the
[actual half-turn sectors](fdip-000L) whenever two is invertible.
Their sign, support parity and group degree record distinct structures.}
\p{Over the reals, an orthogonal involution commuting with positive
precision gives a [product law](fdip-000M). Restricting the Schur
map and taking the [retained marginal](fdip-003R) are compatible
with those sectors. The [four-cycle calculation](fdip-003S)
recovers every normalizer and covariance, while its
[commutant](fdip-003T) explains the remaining freedom.
[Characteristic two](fdip-000N) tests the coefficient boundary.}

\transclude{fdip-003N}
